{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"1968","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"D. Permutation Game"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"2 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Bodya and Sasha found a permutation $$$p_1,\\dots,p_n$$$ and an array $$$a_1,\\dots,a_n$$$. They decided to play a well-known \"Permutation game\"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"A permutation of length $$$n$$$ is an array consisting of $$$n$$$ distinct integers from $$$1$$$ to $$$n$$$ in arbitrary order. For example, $$$[2,3,1,5,4]$$$ is a permutation, but $$$[1,2,2]$$$ is not a permutation ($$$2$$$ appears twice in the array), and $$$[1,3,4]$$$ is also not a permutation ($$$n=3$$$ but there is $$$4$$$ in the array)."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Both of them chose a starting position in the permutation."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The game lasts $$$k$$$ turns. The players make moves simultaneously. On each turn, two things happen to each player: "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" If the current position of the player is $$$x$$$, his score increases by $$$a_x$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" Then the player either "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"stays"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" at his current position $$$x$$$ or "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"moves"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" from $$$x$$$ to $$$p_x$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"kind":"text","text":" The winner of the game is the player with the higher score after exactly $$$k$$$ turns."},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Knowing Bodya's starting position $$$P_B$$$ and Sasha's starting position $$$P_S$$$, determine who wins the game if both players are trying to win."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line contains a single integer $$$t$$$ ($$$1\\le t\\le 10^4$$$) — the number of testcases."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line of each testcase contains integers $$$n$$$, $$$k$$$, $$$P_B$$$, $$$P_S$$$ ($$$1\\le P_B,P_S\\le n\\le 2\\cdot 10^5$$$, $$$1\\le k\\le 10^9$$$) — length of the permutation, duration of the game, starting positions respectively."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The next line contains $$$n$$$ integers $$$p_1,\\dots,p_n$$$ ($$$1 \\le p_i \\le n$$$) — elements of the permutation $$$p$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The next line contains $$$n$$$ integers $$$a_1,\\dots,a_n$$$ ($$$1\\le a_i\\le 10^9$$$) — elements of array $$$a$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"It is guaranteed that the sum of values of $$$n$$$ over all test cases does not exceed $$$2 \\cdot 10^5$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For each testcase output: "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Bodya"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" if Bodya wins the game. "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Sasha"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" if Sasha wins the game. "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Draw"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" if the players have the same score. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Example"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n10\n4 2 3 2\n4 1 2 3\n7 2 5 6\n10 8 2 10\n3 1 4 5 2 7 8 10 6 9\n5 10 5 1 3 7 10 15 4 3\n2 1000000000 1 2\n1 2\n4 4\n8 10 4 1\n5 1 4 3 2 8 6 7\n1 1 2 1 2 100 101 102\n5 1 2 5\n1 2 4 5 3\n4 6 9 4 2\n4 2 3 1\n4 1 3 2\n6 8 5 3\n6 9 5 4\n6 1 3 5 2 4\n6 9 8 9 5 10\n4 8 4 2\n2 3 4 1\n5 2 8 7\n4 2 3 1\n4 1 3 2\n6 8 5 3\n2 1000000000 1 2\n1 2\n1000000000 2\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\nBodya\nSasha\nDraw\nDraw\nBodya\nSasha\nSasha\nSasha\nSasha\nBodya\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Below you can find the explanation for the first testcase, where the game consists of $$$k=2$$$ turns."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"attrs":{"header":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Turn"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"table_cell"},{"attrs":{"header":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Bodya's position"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"table_cell"},{"attrs":{"header":false},"children":[{"